course: dictionary
lesson: 12934
title: Words about leaving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Evict means to force someone to leave the place where they live or stay. It usually happens when a tenant does not pay rent or breaks the rules, and the landlord must follow the law. «The landlord wants to evict the family because they have not paid rent for three months.» The clues are force, leave and rent.
explain: The word also works in nature. «The cuckoo chick evicts the other eggs from the nest.» The chick pushes the other eggs out, so they can no longer stay there. Ask yourself: is someone or something being made to leave? If yes, evict fits.
explain: Look for the phrases «be evicted», «evict the tenants» and «an eviction notice», which is a written warning that you must leave. Evict is a verb, so it changes: evicts, evicted, evicting.
fact: Evict means to force someone to leave a home or a place.
fact: Evict is a verb: evict, evicts, evicted, evicting.
fact: Eviction is the noun, meaning the act of forcing someone to leave.
fact: A landlord must follow the law before they can evict a tenant.
fact: Animals can be evicted too, such as when a cuckoo chick evicts the other eggs from a nest.
exercise: «The landlord said he would evict the family after they missed six months of rent.» What does evict mean here? | *Force them to leave their home | Give them a free house | Invite them to dinner | Paint the front door
exercise: «The cuckoo chick evicts the other eggs from the nest.» What happens to the other eggs? | They are kept warm under the bird | They are sold at the market | They are hatched into chicks | *They are pushed out of the nest
exercise: Which word is the noun for the act of forcing someone out of their home? | *eviction | evicted | evicts | evicting
test: «The tenants found an eviction notice on their door.» What is an eviction notice? | *A written warning that you must leave | A bill for the electricity | A party invitation | A map of the town
test: Complete the sentence: The family was ___ because they broke the rules of the building. | evicts | evicting | *evicted | evict
exam: Which sentence uses evict correctly? | *The council can evict tenants who do not pay their rent | The bird evicts a lovely song every morning | The teacher evicts the sunshine from the classroom | The baker evicts fresh bread from the oven
